7. Rewrite the following `while` loop using an equivalent `for` loop in Java:
```java
int count = 10;
while (count >= 2) {
    System.out.println(count);
    count -= 2;
}
```

questions.answer:
**Equivalent Java `for` loop:**
```java
for (int count = 10; count >= 2; count -= 2) {
    System.out.println(count);
}
```
**Output:** Prints `10`, `8`, `6`, `4`, `2` on separate lines.

